{
  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_008: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer, weighted → 0.573 acc, 6.61 GPU-hrs), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality is actually contributing to performance or whether the RNA signal alone suffices. config_029 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, transformer) isolates this by removing the image encoder while keeping the same RNA encoder and transformer aggregation, making it a clean ablation. If RNA-only approaches or exceeds 0.573, the search can pivot toward cheaper unimodal or simpler multimodal configs; if it falls well short, multimodal fusion is confirmed as essential and I can focus remaining budget on optimizing image encoder and fusion strategy. Expected relative cost: roughly 3–4 GPU hours (no image encoder, but retains transformer aggregation and multiprofile processing), about half of config_008, preserving budget for subsequent experiments."
}

